      "side": 1,
      "message": "Slight correction: Per PD r3.2 v1.1 ss 5.9.2, the number of Data Objects in a BIST Test Data message should be 7. I don\u0027t think that actually matters at the TCPCI driver layer, but it would be nice to use a valid message. I htink your size was only off by 1.\n\nSo\n* The header should be `PD_HEADER(..., /*cnt\u003d*/7, ...)`\n* `buf` should be `uint8_t buf[sizeof(input_header) + sizeof(input_bdo) * 7] \u003d {0};`, which should end up being 32 like in the example I linked.\n* I guess you should initialize the rest of `buf` to 0 as above. The actual contents of the Data Objects 2-7 shouldn\u0027t matter for the test, but its probably best if they\u0027re initialized deterministically.",
      "parentUuid": "bf6e34fa_28fbab03",
